.TH qsh-identity-move-key 1  "move-key 0.5.3" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-identity\-move\-key \- Move this device\*(Aqs private key to another key store (`file` or `platform`) without changing the device id, certificate or fingerprint, so peers\*(Aq pins and ACL rows stay valid (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0032). A local command: it cannot be run against a remote host. Run it before an always\-on service (a LaunchDaemon, systemd linger) if the OS credential store is not reachable from there, as `qsh doctor` reports
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh identity move\-key\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move this device\*(Aqs private key to another key store (`file` or `platform`) without changing the device id, certificate or fingerprint, so peers\*(Aq pins and ACL rows stay valid (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0032). A local command: it cannot be run against a remote host. Run it before an always\-on service (a LaunchDaemon, systemd linger) if the OS credential store is not reachable from there, as `qsh doctor` reports
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<STORE>\fR
The store the private key should live in afterwards: `file` (`identity/device.key`, mode 0600) or `platform` (the OS credential store). A key that already lives there is left alone
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.5.3
